-- title:
--   Hecke–Galois datum from a cube-free residual modularity witness
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime and let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$ with $\Delta_W \neq 0$ which is a semistable model, in the sense that no prime $q$ dividing $\Delta_W$ divides $c_4(W)$, and whose mod $p$ representation is irreducible, meaning that the $p$-torsion of $W$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ is nontrivial and its only Galois-stable $\mathbb{Z}/p$-submodules are $0$ and the whole module. Let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $p^2 \nmid M$ and with $q^3 \nmid M$ for every prime $q \neq p$, and assume $W$ is residually modular of level $M$: there are a normalised eigenform $f$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(M)$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}$ in $\mathbb{C}$ containing $p$ such that for each prime $\ell \neq p$ with $\ell \nmid M$ and $\ell \nmid \Delta_W$ the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $f$ is an algebraic integer congruent to $a_\ell(W) = \ell + 1 - \#W(\mathbb{F}_\ell)$ modulo $\mathfrak{m}$. Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring with finite residue field and with $p$ in its maximal ideal. Then there exist a finite set $S$ of primes containing $p$ and every prime $q$ with $q \mid \Delta_W$, and a nonzero level $N$, such that every prime dividing $N$ lies in $S$; for each $q \in S$ with $q \neq p$ one has $q^2 \mid N$ and $q^3 \nmid N$; if $p \mid \Delta_W$ or $p \nmid a_p(W)$ then $p \mid N$ and $p^2 \nmid N$, while if $p \nmid \Delta_W$ and $p \mid a_p(W)$ then $p \nmid N$; the space of weight-$2$ cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ is spanned over $\mathbb{C}$ by the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of the forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients are rational integers; there is a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ together with the $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S$, to the residue field of $\mathcal{O}$, with $\theta(T_\ell)$ the residue of $a_\ell(W)$ for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$; and there is a complete noetherian local ring $T$, an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra along a local homomorphism, finite and free as an $\mathcal{O}$-module, carrying a [`CuspForm.HeckeGaloisRepDatum`](def/CuspForm_HeckeGaloisRepDatum.html#L8) for $(N, S, \mathcal{O}, \theta)$: a ring homomorphism $\pi$ from the Hecke algebra to $T$ whose reduction is $\theta$, with $T$ generated over $\mathcal{O}$ by the image of $\pi$ and with residue map surjective on $\mathcal{O}$, such that every $\mathcal{O}$-valued eigensystem reducing to $\theta$ factors through $\pi$ by an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra map, together with a rank-$2$ adically continuous Galois representation $\rho$ over $T$ whose Frobenius elements at primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ have characteristic polynomial $X^2 - \pi(T_\ell)X + \ell$ and whose residual representation is absolutely irreducible.
--
--   This is the step that converts residual modularity of a semistable elliptic curve, witnessed at a level not divisible by $p^2$ and cube-free away from $p$, into the Hecke-algebra-plus-Galois-representation input of the Taylor–Wiles argument, with the $p$-part of the level normalised to the ordinary or the flat shape and the level away from $p$ of exponent exactly two. It feeds the construction of the patching datum over a finite extension of $\mathcal{O}$.
